item.descriptionText:
A restful retreat that&rsquo;s grand yet intimate &ndash; and serene on every level &ndash; Lanson Place Causeway Bay, Hong Kong blends the warmth of Hong Kong hospitality with chic, French influences. After all, this luxury hotel has been reimagined by acclaimed designer Pierre-Yves Rochon. Inside, expect light-filled spaces, refined dining and little touches that pay homage to craftsmanship.<br>
<br>
From check-in to stepping out, Lanson Place is an invitation to unwind &ndash; with no request too big or detail too small. Salon Lanson continues the Parisian elegance, transforming from daytime bistro to cool nightspot, serving signature cocktails. While in the refined rooms and suites, a curated pillow menu, calming spa music and soothing essential oils are just a handful of the thoughtful touches. Perfect after days spent exploring Hong Kong.&nbsp;&nbsp;

On the shores of Beijing&rsquo;s Yanqi Lake, enveloped by gardens, Yanbai Villa by Wild Goose &amp; Pine is a tranquil &ndash; and luxurious &ndash; escape from the city lights. There&rsquo;s beauty to see here all year round as the landscape reflects the changing seasons. And the hotel&rsquo;s been designed by renowned Pritzker prize-winning architect Wang Shu to immerse you in the sights, sounds and scents of nature, from woods to hills and waterfalls.<br>
<br>
Shu was inspired by the Song Dynasty paintings &lsquo;A Panorama of Rivers and Mountains&rsquo;, and &lsquo;Landscapes of the Four Seasons&rsquo; when planning Yanbai Villa&rsquo;s design. It&rsquo;s no surprise that the hotel&rsquo;s 27,000m&sup2; of gardens are its highlight &ndash; dotted with trees, bridges and zig-zagging trails for refreshing strolls. Observation decks and terraces allow you to take in panoramic views of serene Yanqi Lake, and the striking wooded slopes of Yanqi Island. While the hotel&rsquo;s rooms invite the outside in, nestled within the gardens and featuring floor-to-ceiling windows framing rustling leaves or shimmering water. Interiors have an elegant aesthetic &ndash; and every creature comfort &ndash; with neutral colours, smooth wood panelling and understated murals.&nbsp;

Channelling the peace, balance and tranquillity of the Hubei region&rsquo;s lush countryside, INTO Hotel Chibi offers an oasis of calm and quiet luxury. Find true escape from the strains of modern life, tucked away amid swaying bamboo forests and Jiangnan gardens. Balancing traditional heritage with contemporary charm, the hotel&rsquo;s palette of calming neutrals and natural materials is paired with sleek minimalism, creating the ultimate setting for a relaxing retreat.<br>
<br>
Choose from a range of immaculately presented suites, each offering unique aspects, from stunning forest or garden views to cosy log cabin ambience. Expect high ceilings, deep soaking tubs and delicate Le Labo fragrances throughout. Make time for quiet reflection in the communal Book Gallery, or enjoy a ceremonial tasting (and panoramic views) in the hotel&rsquo;s private mountainside Tea House.&nbsp;

People have been drawn to the natural wilderness for centuries, but always crave a haven during their adventures. Set amongst thousands of years of Silk Road heritage, Jangala Dunhuang perfectly encapsulates this search for sanctuary. Rooted in the Sanskrit-derived word for &lsquo;oasis&rsquo;, this boutique hotel&rsquo;s entire ethos &ndash; from its Gobi Desert backdrop to its beautiful rooms and suites &ndash; puts guests at the heart of the natural world and its hidden marvels.<br>
<br>
As the first of its kind in Dunhuang, this hotel sets a new standard. Inspired by its connection to lively Dunhuang city, it also celebrates modern creativity and local traditions. The Living Room fuses minimalist marble d&eacute;cor with cosy sofas, its walls home to art. Outside, the Water View Theatre puts on a range of shows all year round, while the courtyard and oasis view rooms make luxurious exhibits of desert and sky. In between delicious meals in the Silk &amp; Spice restaurant, and cocktails at the world-class Mirage Bar, salute the sun with yoga, take up camp in the desert, or press &lsquo;pause&rsquo; in the hotel&rsquo;s Meditation Space.&nbsp;

Inspired by poetry and nature, The Hanyu Garden Reserve Suzhou&nbsp;is a serene resort perched on the tranquil shores of Lake Taihu. Recreating the elegant charms of garden-city Suzhou, this verdant escape promises a balance of heritage and charm, beauty and peace, all within easy reach of bustling nightlife, local landmarks and authentic culture.&nbsp;<br>
<br>
With low-lying buildings and stunning landscaped gardens, the hotel blends artfully into its lakeside surroundings. Traditional pagodas and peaked roofs punctuate the grounds, where water features and rockeries blend harmoniously with trees and flowers. Inside, the lavish interiors and modern comforts are equally majestic. The hotel has an impressive collection of cultural relics, calligraphy, and historic and modern artworks, acting as museum, gallery and getaway. Both inside and out there are many secluded spaces to sit and reflect, enjoy a drink, or relax with friends.&nbsp;

From the outside the Younch Hotel has a grand, slightly fortress-like edifice &ndash; as if it&rsquo;s taken inspiration from Xi&rsquo;an&rsquo;s impressive ramparts. Inside however, the hotel is anything but austere. The impressive lobby gives way to an architectural dreamland full of muted tones, layered textures and subtle lighting. An oasis of calm, luxury and comfort, and a welcome escape from the hustle and bustle of the city.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>
<br>
Ranging around a central courtyard with a tranquil meditation pool and pared-back planting, sun-filled rooms offer peaceful aspects and cocooning d&eacute;cor. Soak away your cares in a free-standing tub and Aqua di Parma amenities. Or head to the bar where master mixologists weave tales of the thirteen dynasties that ruled the city into signature cocktails.&nbsp;

Bringing a touch of French Romanticism to laid-back Nanzhuang, Miaoli, Grasse Grace Manor invites you to truly relax. Inspired by the beauty of its namesake, the perfume capital of southern France, the boutique&rsquo;s architecture is grandly Gothic in style. While its interiors are calm, cool and as luxurious as you&rsquo;d expect.&nbsp;<br>
<br>
Grasse Grace Manor&rsquo;s bedrooms are a masterclass in serenity. Panelled walls, ornate bedheads and gilt-framed mirrors are balanced with soft washes of soothing blues and pastels. Large windows reveal the lush green hills surrounding the hotel, and bathe the rooms in light. The communal spaces meanwhile dial up the opulence&nbsp;&ndash; from the next-level marble foyer to the Gothic arches and chandeliers of Jasmine restaurant. The art and craft of high-end French gastronomy is celebrated here &ndash; sink into long, lavish dining experiences, each dish a treat for the eyes as well as the palate.&nbsp;

Nestled on the tranquil shores of Taiwan&rsquo;s largest alpine lake, Hotel Beore Sun Moon Lake is a true slice of solace. Designed to highlight its sweeping mountain views, and put the serene landscape into the spotlight, you&rsquo;re never far from Taipei&rsquo;s city buzz, while being perfectly placed for low-key adventures and luxurious seclusion.&nbsp;<br>
<br>
The hotel&rsquo;s muted tones, antique stone and kiln-fired tile details create a calming feel &ndash; you might just find you breathe a little easier when you step inside. Unwind in modern rooms where comfort, and a restful night, are key. But it&rsquo;s not only the rooms that are designed for relaxation. When it comes to serenity, Hotel Beore Sun Moon Lake&rsquo;s got you covered &ndash; simply make your way up to the rooftop pool, where you can doze the afternoon away, or unwind in the fully kitted-out media room. The meals in its exclusive restaurant take inspiration from local ingredients &ndash; each dish created by an innovative team to showcase Taiwan&rsquo;s flavours.&nbsp;
